From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 08:25:28 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] uml: report a page fault's P bit to x86 tasks

x86 sets bit 0 of a page fault's error code, P, when the access found a
present page and violated its protection: a store to a page mapped
read-only has error code 7, and an instruction fetch from a present page
without execute permission 0x15. P is clear when the page was not there,
as for a PROT_NONE page (4 for a load, 6 for a store, 0x14 for a fetch).
The Darwin host reports only the access kind, so a task's SIGSEGV
handler read 6 and 0x14 for both cases.

When a fault is to be delivered to an x86 task, segv() now looks the
page up in the task's page tables and sets P in the error code the
signal frame carries when the page is present. A PROT_NONE page is not
present to x86's hardware, and UML marks it with _PAGE_PROTNONE alone.
An Intel Xeon Platinum 8581C reports the same codes for the same
accesses.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/um/kernel/trap.c | 53 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 53 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/um/kernel/trap.c b/arch/um/kernel/trap.c
index 5e9fd804f83a415c87a74bffca82986c10db8a8e..716e4661a52bee59916abecb848be9d647a53b21 100644
--- a/arch/um/kernel/trap.c
+++ b/arch/um/kernel/trap.c
@@ -269,6 +269,47 @@ int handle_uaccess_fault(unsigned long address, int is_write, int *code_out)
 					code_out);
 }
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_UML_X86_64_USERSPACE_ONLY
+/* The P bit of an x86 page fault's error code: the access violated the
+ * protection of a page the task has mapped, as opposed to touching one it
+ * has not. */
+#define UML_X86_PF_PROT 1
+
+/*
+ * Whether the task has a present page at the address, for the P bit. A
+ * PROT_NONE page is not present to x86's hardware, whatever the generic
+ * pte_present() says of it.
+ */
+static bool user_page_present(struct mm_struct *mm, unsigned long address)
+{
+	pgd_t *pgd;
+	p4d_t *p4d;
+	pud_t *pud;
+	pmd_t *pmd;
+	pte_t *pte;
+	bool present = false;
+
+	mmap_read_lock(mm);
+	pgd = pgd_offset(mm, address);
+	if (pgd_none(*pgd))
+		goto out;
+	p4d = p4d_offset(pgd, address);
+	if (p4d_none(*p4d))
+		goto out;
+	pud = pud_offset(p4d, address);
+	if (pud_none(*pud))
+		goto out;
+	pmd = pmd_offset(pud, address);
+	if (pmd_none(*pmd) || pmd_bad(*pmd))
+		goto out;
+	pte = pte_offset_kernel(pmd, address);
+	present = pte_get_bits(*pte, _PAGE_PRESENT) != 0;
+out:
+	mmap_read_unlock(mm);
+	return present;
+}
+#endif
+
 static void show_segv_info(struct uml_pt_regs *regs)
 {
 	struct task_struct *tsk = current;
@@ -465,6 +506,18 @@ unsigned long segv(struct faultinfo fi, unsigned long ip, int is_user,
 	}
 	show_segv_info(regs);
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_UML_X86_64_USERSPACE_ONLY
+	/*
+	 * The host reports no P bit: a fault the task is to see, on a page it
+	 * has present, is a protection violation of it. The signal frame takes
+	 * its error code from the task's registers, not from this copy.
+	 */
+	if (user_page_present(current->mm, address)) {
+		fi.error_code |= UML_X86_PF_PROT;
+		if (regs)
+			UPT_FAULTINFO(regs)->error_code |= UML_X86_PF_PROT;
+	}
+#endif
 	if (err == -EACCES) {
 		current->thread.arch.faultinfo = fi;
 		force_sig_fault(SIGBUS, BUS_ADRERR, (void __user *)address);
